WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.950
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.770
Let's go, Kusanagi.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.680
To where?

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.550
To Revolver.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.930
You're Revolver.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.900
Playmaker...

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:15.490
So you found this place.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.460
I'm Ryoken Kokami.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.070
Dr. Kogami's son.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.070
Revolver, tell the truth.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.540
That's what we're after.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.170
We have the right to know.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.680
You said the Lost Incident 
was to create the Ignis.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.650
But why would you have to go this far?

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:42.890
My father didn't create the Ignis 
to cause chaos in the world.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:51.360
To oppose the danger facing humanity, my 
father's goal was to create humanity's successor.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:56.600
But my father began to feel 
anxious about his research.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:03.810
Using the Ignis's Data Material, 
he created a super computer.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.810
To analyze and predict the Ignis's growth.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.950
And the result was surprising.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.920
The end of humanity.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.120
End of humanity?

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:23.830
The Ignis will develop rapidly and 
erase humanity in the process.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.540
Right now, we must do whatever 
it takes to kill the Ignis!

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:34.340
This all started because of Dr. 
Kogami's crazy plan ten years ago!

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:40.460
We've been manipulated by an 
illusion from ten years ago.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.810
We don't need to be anymore!

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.550
In order to walk a new path, stop 
the Tower of Hanoi, Revolver!

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.420
You have the wrong idea about me.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:53.890
I'm not a good person!

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:59.200
If you want to stop the Tower 
of Hanoi, there's only one way.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.170
By defeating me!

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.140
We really have to fight?

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.370
Don't annoy me.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.840
Into the VRAINS!

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.710
I run Across the universe

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.880
At the speed of light

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.750
Begin Loading

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.480
Open the door of dreams

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.050
VRAINS spreads

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.160
Believe in myself

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:46.690
VRAINS continues

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:52.000
The circuit draws the future

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.070
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.670
Access!

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.370
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:01.970
I'm now With the Wind

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.280
Link with my soul

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.050
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.780
Now Win the Race

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.620
Connected world

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:15.120
No matter when

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:18.490
Nothing is impossible

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:22.630
Strive for hope

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.200
And ride the wind!

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.250
They already started.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.720
Good luck, Yusaku!

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.690
Okay!  Go!

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:09.300
Boss!  It's taking all I 
have to avoid this rubble!

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.630
Boss!  We made it through safely!

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.900
Not safely for me.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:24.640
You avoided it, but they all hit me.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.880
I'm sorry!

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:34.100
The Tower of Hanoi will be 
completed in less than an hour.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:39.280
Playmaker, we must stop it!

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:40.730
Yeah.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.700
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:51.490
Link Coin Special Summons the monster 
I sent to the graveyard last turn.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:54.420
Resurrect, Voritcular Drumgon!

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.750
Voritcular Drumgon's effect activates.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:03.200
When it's Special Summoned, I draw one card!

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.400
And I summon Sniffer Dragon from my hand!

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.620
Sniffer Dragon's effect activates!

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:19.330
When it's summoned, I add Sniffer 
Dragon from my deck to my hand.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.920
Voritcular Drumgon is Link 3.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.930
And since he summoned another monster...

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.570
A Link 4 monster is coming!

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:33.550
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:36.150
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.850
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:46.660
I set Sniffer Dragon and Link 3 
Voritcular Drumgon in the Link Markers!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:49.760
Link Summon!

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:59.230
Appear, Link 4 Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.860
There it is!

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:08.950
From my hand, I activate the 
Equip Spell, Borrel Regenerator!

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:15.890
I Special Summon a Rokket from my graveyard 
in defense position and equip it with this card.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:19.390
I Special Summon Metalrokket Dragon!

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:28.340
Then due to the Field Spell, 
Boot Sector Launch...

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:32.730
...Rokkets gain 300 ATK and DEF.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:37.670
Damn!  I knew he'd summon next to its link!

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.440
Here it comes, Playmaker!

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.810
Now Topologic Bomber's effect.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:47.520
When a monster is Special Summoned 
next to a Link Monster's link...

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:52.040
...all monsters in our Main 
Monster Zones are destroyed!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.080
Full Overlap!

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:03.760
Now you have no monsters to protect you.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.610
Are you sure?

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.570
What?

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:16.010
Restoration Point Guard isn't destroyed when 
another Link Monster is Link Summoned that turn.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.910
I see.  Well, fine.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.980
In that case, Borrel Regenerator's effect.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:28.590
When the equipped monster is destroyed, 
I draw one card from my deck!

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:29.940
Let's battle!

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:34.070
Topologic Bomber attacks 
Restoration Point Guard!

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:38.070
Ultimate Malicious Code!

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:41.430
What'll you do, Playmaker?

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:46.680
Restoration Point Guard won't be 
destroyed, but it only has 1000 ATK.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.880
We'll take 2000 damage!

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:49.910
I know.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:53.790
I activate Rescue Interlacer's 
effect from my hand!

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:57.510
When a Cyberse in attack 
position is attacked...

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:02.330
...I discard this card to 
drop the battle damage to 0!

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.630
So you also stopped this attack.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.170
But you'll take Topologic Bomber's effect.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:18.120
You take damage equal to your 
attacked monster's original ATK!

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.000
Aiming Blast!

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:29.140
Sheesh!  He keeps shaving away our LP!

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:32.430
But you managed to keep the damage down.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:35.860
No.  He still has a set card.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.130
Exactly, Playmaker.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:43.110
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Mirror Force Launcher.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:50.760
I discard one card to add Mirror 
Force from my graveyard to my hand.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.340
What?  Mirror Force is coming back?

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.480
This is really bad!

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:01.070
I set two cards!

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:04.990
I activate the effect of the Metalrokket 
that I sent to the graveyard!

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:09.260
I Special Summon a different 
Rokket from my deck!

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:12.870
I Special Summon Magnarokket Dragon!

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:17.000
I end my turn.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.970
Rescue Interlacer's effect 
activates from the graveyard!

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:25.960
When it uses its effect, it Special Summons 
itself from the graveyard at the end of the turn.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.980
Resurrect, Rescue Interlacer!

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:37.920
Yusaku, you made comebacks in duels 
that everyone thought you'd lose.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.930
Defeat Revolver!

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:47.370
Revolver is doubly ready with 
Topologic and Mirror Force!

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:53.340
Yeah.  The next turn will be tough, 
but do your best, Playmaker!

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.700
What are you going to do?

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:59.580
One of his set cards is 
definitely Mirror Force.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.820
You're right.  His formation 
is truly powerful.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:07.000
But there is a way to break it.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.390
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.940
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:15.550
What?

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:19.040
Link Summoning is a bad 
matchup against Mirror Force!

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.730
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:27.710
I set Rescue Interlacer and Link 2 
Restoration Point Guard in the Link Markers!

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:29.670
Link Summon!

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:34.110
Appear, Link 3 Transcode Talker!

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:45.790
Transcode Talker's effect activates!

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:51.810
I Special Summon a Code Talker from 
my graveyard next to its link!

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:55.000
Resurrect, Excode Talker!

00:10:56.730 --> 00:11:01.140
Like I said...  If you summon a monster 
next to its link when he has Topologic-

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.450
Excode Talker?

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.350
Excode Talker's effect!

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:14.790
The monster linked to this card gains 500 ATK 
and can't be destroyed by your cards' effects!

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:18.790
But Excode Talker will be destroyed!

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:23.260
Exactly!  Topologic Bomber's 
effect now activates!

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.160
Full Overlap!

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:29.200
I activate the trap, Shield Handler!

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.210
When a monster-destroying effect activates, 
a Link Monster's effects are negated!

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:39.480
A card that seals Topologic 
Bomber's effects...

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:41.180
That's not all.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:44.620
After Shield Handler activates, 
it becomes an Equip Card.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:48.370
The equipped monster can't 
be destroyed by card effects.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.760
I equip this card on Excode Talker!

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:59.930
Due to Transcode Talker's effect, 
Transcode and Excode gain ATK!

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:04.400
Not only can't Excode or Transcode 
be destroyed by effects...

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:08.670
...Transcode now has more 
ATK than Topologic Bomber!

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:11.290
Impressive, Playmaker.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:14.550
You greatly sealed away my offense.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:18.470
You won't talk so big anymore!

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:21.120
All right!  Attack with Transcode Talker-

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:21.860
Not yet!

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:24.160
You'll do something else?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.260
I'll end this now!

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:31.200
I return ROM Cloudia from my graveyard to 
my hand and Special Summon SIMM Tablir!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:41.410
I can Special Summon it from my hand next to 
the link of a monster that's already linked!

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:44.380
And I summon ROM Cloudia!

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:52.850
When it's summoned, I can add one Cyberse 
monster from my graveyard to my hand.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:56.330
I add Latency to my hand!

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.560
Latency's effect activates!

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:04.760
Once per turn, I can Special Summon it when 
it's added to my hand from my graveyard!

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:06.880
Come, Latency!

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:13.140
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:17.210
The summoning conditions are three monsters!

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:22.900
I set SIMM Tablir, ROM Cloudia 
and Latency in the Link Markers!

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:24.680
Circuit combine!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.150
Link Summon!

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:30.590
Appear, Link 3 Powercode Talker!

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.200
Latency's additional effect!

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.180
When it's Special Summoned 
due to its own effect and

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:46.060
then used to Link Summon, I draw one card!

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:48.660
Then Excode Talker's effect!

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:54.220
Monsters next to its links gain 500 
ATK and can't be destroyed by effects!

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:58.590
Wow!  Three Link Monsters!

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:01.390
And all three can't be destroyed by effects!

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:02.820
We have nothing to fear!

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:06.790
Revolver has two monsters and 3000 LP.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:09.760
If all our attacks get through, we win!

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.840
Here I go!  Let's battle!

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:21.070
Playmaker turned this 
fight completely around!

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:25.510
I knew that he would!  Playmaker!

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.510
Protect our network world!

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:31.250
Here I go!  Let's battle!

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:35.650
Powercode Talker attacks Magnarokket!

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.880
Power Termination Smash!

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:52.300
All right!  The first attack went through!

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.040
Keep pressing!

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:55.770
Transcode Talker!

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.580
Attack Topologic Bomber!

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:07.550
Will you succeed?

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:11.880
I now activate the Continuous 
Trap, Link Turret!

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.470
What's that?

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:27.660
Playmaker, I expected you to create 
a strategy against Topologic.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:32.410
I send two Rokket monsters 
in my deck to the graveyard.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:37.880
I place a Rokket Counter on this card for 
every Link 3 or higher monster on the field.

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:42.220
And my Link Monsters can't be 
destroyed in battle this turn.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:45.320
Damn!  A card that negates destruction!

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.690
But you still take damage.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:51.000
Go!  Trans Fault!

00:15:57.030 --> 00:16:01.610
There are currently four Link 3 
or higher monsters on the field.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:06.340
So I place four Rokket 
Counters on Link Turret.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.710
Something weird has appeared.

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:12.780
Now for Link Turret's additional effect!

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:19.580
When I take battle damage, I place 
one Rokket Counter on Link Turret.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:24.830
I set one card and end my turn!

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:29.570
The effect of the Magnarokket 
destroyed in battle!

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:34.900
I Special Summon a different 
Rokket from my deck.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:37.910
I Special Summon Autorokket Dragon!

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:45.640
Umm, Playmaker...

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:50.590
Five counters seem really dangerous.

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:55.330
Did you get carried away and attack too much?

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:56.590
Maybe.

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:59.330
If Revolver summons it now...

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:06.650
You seem to know what will happen next.

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:13.310
Playmaker, you're the one 
who fell for my strategy.

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:15.710
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:19.150
From my hand, I activate the 
Quick-Play Spell, Squib Draw!

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:25.590
I destroy a Rokket on my 
field to draw two cards.

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:30.590
I destroy Autorokket and 
draw two cards from my deck!

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:34.330
Then the Field Spell, Boot 
Sector Launch's effect.

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:38.740
When you have more monsters than me...

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:44.120
...I Special Summon Rokkets from my 
graveyard in defense position equal to the difference.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.620
You have two more monsters than me.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:52.010
So I Special Summon 
Shelrokket and Metalrokket!

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:59.390
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:02.230
Arrowheads confirmed.

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:06.030
The summoning conditions are two Rokkets!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.170
Link Summon!

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:13.170
Appear, Link 2 Miniborrel Dragon!

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:18.330
And I summon Gateway Dragon!

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.950
Its effect activates!

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:26.050
I can Special Summon a Level 4 
or lower monster from my hand.

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:28.900
I Special Summon Sniffer Dragon!

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:35.950
This means...  It's coming!

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:40.970
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.940
The summoning conditions are 
at least three Effect Monsters!

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:52.580
I set Gateway, Sniffer and Link 
2 Miniborrel in the Link Markers!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.050
Circuit combine!

00:18:55.410 --> 00:19:01.420
Playmaker!  This is the bullet 
that will decide our destiny!

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:03.420
Link Summon!

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:10.360
Manifest, Link 4 Borreload Dragon!

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:20.130
His incredible dragon appeared!

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:25.210
But we have higher ATK!

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:28.450
You're an AI, but you 
can't remember anything?

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:31.450
You've forgotten Borreload's effect.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:33.920
What was it again?

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:36.120
I'll tell you!

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:38.920
Learn overwhelming despair!

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:40.660
Borreload's effect!

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:46.660
Once per turn, I lower one 
monster's ATK and DEF by 500!

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:51.240
You can't activate your effects 
against this effect's activation!

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:59.180
Borreload attacks Transcode Talker!

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:04.520
You're attacking?  Your monster has 
3000 ATK while ours has 3300 ATK!

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.770
Borreload's effect!

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:08.970
When it attacks your monster...

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:13.760
...your monster is placed next to 
Borreload's link, and I gain control of it!

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:15.950
Strange Trigger!

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:27.440
I remember this effect now!

00:20:27.860 --> 00:20:31.600
Since Transcode Talker 
switched to my field...

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:36.060
...Excode Talker loses its 
effect, so it loses 500 ATK.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:39.420
Then Transcode Talker's effect.

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:46.900
When this card is mutually linked, 
both monsters gain 500 ATK!

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:50.460
Go, Topologic Bomber!

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:52.500
Attack Excode Talker!

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:56.230
Ultimate Malicious Code!

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:09.750
Excode Talker's effect vanishes, 
so Powercode Talker loses 500 ATK.

00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:15.460
Next, Transcode Talker 
attacks Powercode Talker!

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:27.200
Yusaku!

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:29.200
Playmaker!

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:31.100
He's strong...

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:40.290
Seriously?  All our monsters were destroyed.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:42.880
Playmaker!

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:46.560
There isn't a new path left for us.

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:53.290
We are prisoners of destiny, 
chained by the past ten years ago.

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:54.860
Therefore...

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:57.700
I will sever everything now!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:15.000
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:22.140
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:29.340
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:36.720
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:37.550 --> 00:22:43.940
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:48.090
There were fragments of power

00:22:48.330 --> 00:22:55.270
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:55.500 --> 00:23:02.610
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:02.740 --> 00:23:09.820
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.050 --> 00:23:17.020
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:23.900
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:31.570
Lighting Life with our invisible bond

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:39.940
Seasoned duelists don't miss their 
chance to finish their opponents.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:45.660
When Playmaker's impregnable defense 
is broken, Revolver quietly says...

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:48.290
This is the end.

00:23:48.290 --> 00:23:54.990
When the two Extra Monster Zones connect, a 
power that transcends knowledge manifests!

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:58.630
A card that surpasses Mirror 
Force...  Can it be?

00:23:58.630 --> 00:24:02.370
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Duel in the Extreme Domain

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:04.430
Into the VRAINS!
